astronomers now know that there are  billions of exoplanets in our galaxy  waiting to be discovered  but knowing they're there and finding  them are very different things the  problem with finding exoplanets is that  a plant is so tiny and so dim compared  to a star that it's essentially  undetectable unless you get very clever  one of the things you can do is you can  actually see that there's a  gravitational pull between a star and a  planet as amazing as it sounds as a  planet orbits a star  it'll tug on it gravitationally and the  star will wobble a little bit and you  can detect that  some of the first exoplanets were  discovered by looking for wobbling stars  but now there's a more effective way to  find these distant worlds perhaps more a  direct way of seeing exoplanets is by  the transit method in this case the  planet and the star lineup right exactly  in our view so that the planet goes  across the star making a tiny little  solar eclipse so we actually just find  that the star darkens in a pattern every  time this planet goes round  astronomers have used these methods to  find thousands of exoplanets  [Music]
 

